{%- comment -%}
  XERO popup — DELIBERATELY EMPTY. Retired at the owner's request.

  This section rendered a full-screen entry banner over a photo, once per
  browser session, with an auto-close timer. It is gone. Do not restore it
  without being asked.

  The file stays because the Admin API cannot delete theme files, only
  overwrite them, and because `popup` is still listed in the homepage
  template's section order - an empty section renders nothing and is
  harmless there, whereas a missing section type is an error. The preset is
  removed too, so it can no longer be added from the theme editor.

  Two things about the old behaviour, recorded because they caused real
  confusion and would cause it again:

  1. In the THEME EDITOR the popup showed on every single reload and never
     auto-closed. That was intentional - `window.Shopify.designMode` bypassed
     both the once-per-session check and the auto-close timer so the card
     could be styled. It made the popup look broken when it was not: on the
     live storefront it appeared once per session and dismissed itself.

  2. Its earlier failure to auto-close on phones was real and separate. A
     pointerdown listener sat on the full-screen overlay and cleared the
     auto-close timer, and because opening the popup locked page scroll, a
     visitor's first instinct - to swipe - landed on that overlay and killed
     the timer. Any future overlay in this theme must listen on the card, not
     the scrim.

  The full previous implementation is in git history if it is ever wanted.
{%- endcomment -%}

